Package: personnelSelectionUtility
Title: Utility Analysis Methods for Personnel Selection
Version: 0.5.18
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "René", family = "Gempp", email = "rene.gempp@udp.cl",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0427-6894",
                       affiliation = "Facultad de Administración y Economía, Universidad Diego Portales",
                       web = "https://gempp.cl"))
    )
Description: Implements classical and contemporary utility-analysis methods for
    personnel selection. The package covers Taylor-Russell classification models,
    the Thomas-Owen-Gunst multivariate extension for conjunctive multiple-hurdle
    selection, equal-cutoff solutions for target joint selection ratios, finite
    binomial sampling probabilities, Naylor-Shine expected criterion gains,
    Brogden-Cronbach-Gleser monetary utility, Schmidt-Hunter-Pearlman intervention
    utility, Boudreau-style discounted utility, Sturman-style incremental validity
    for multiple predictors and multiple outcomes, composite effect sizes,
    simulation tools for compensatory and staged multiple-hurdle systems,
    sensitivity analysis, multi-attribute utility, Pareto frontiers, basic
    adverse-impact summaries, AUC-to-effect-size conversion helpers, SDy
    estimation helpers, and diagnostic utilities.
